T+  0.0  The battery in A5 is overheating. The site operator has raised the alarm.
T+  3.5  A5 is venting flammable gas. Its battery is in thermal runaway.
T+  5.8  Pumper 1 on scene.
--- decision 1 at T+5.8: Pumper 1 is the first crew on scene. Time for a first plan.
   [30s, tools: get_situation,get_sensor_check,get_forecast,test_plan,read_lessons,test_plan] Cool A6 and A4 and shelter both communities
     - Pumper 1 cools A6: Pumper 1 can stop spread to the hottest neighbour.
     - Pumper 2 cools A4: Pumper 2 should cool the other close neighbour on arrival.
     - Glenvale homes shelters indoors: Protect Glenvale homes before HF smoke arrives.
     - Glenvale Primary shelters indoors: Protect Glenvale Primary early while smoke direction remains unconfirmed.
     why: Let A5 burn and keep crews upwind beyond 17 metres. Cooling both close neighbours matched cooling B6 with less crew exposure.
     sensor: B6 battery sensor is flat beside the incident, so tests assumed 45 C.
     sensor: The wind meter has no independent smoke drift check.
     sensor: Fixed gas readings are noisy and HAZMAT 1 has not verified them.
     effect: Enclosures involved in 20 minutes: 2.1 -> 1.0
     effect: Peak indoor HF at homes: 0.98 ppm -> 0.2 ppm
T+  5.8  Glenvale homes told to shelter indoors.
T+  5.8  Glenvale Primary told to shelter indoors.
